Z||000000||trigger||07-15-2001||11:11 PM||||Hi,<BR>On Friday the 20th I'm leave Dyersville, Iowa and heading to Sierra Vista, Arizona for a weeks vacation.  Unfortunately I'm taking mom's black 98 Blazer.  It has a dream catcher hanging on the rear view mirror.  Who will I see along the way?  I'll wave if I see any of you.  I'll have the camera and a notebook if I see any Fieros on the way, for sale, in junkyards, or otherwise.  If I could find a deal on a cheap running fixer-upper fiero, I might just get it and drive it home.  LMK if I'm gonna see you along the way.  I don't know our exact route, and I even driving some.  See you on the road.  Thanks.<P>------------------<BR>Honestly officer, I was just keeping up with the flow of traffic.  I know there aren't any cars in the area, that's how far behind I am.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Trigger.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||LAMBO||07-16-2001||01:48 PM||||If you don't mind taking a couple of two lane highways going south through Iowa, take 14 south at the I-80 Newton exit. When you get to Chariton, head west on 34. About two miles out of Chariton, there is a salvage yard on the south side of the highway that has two 87 coupes for sale, sitting out by the road. can't miss em. The black one is a decent driver. The red one is a project. You can then continue on to I-35 at Osceola to get back to interstate. FYI<BR>Todd||||reg||1
